@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-the-clock-is-injected-into-the-task-list
+type: decision-log
+title: "The clock is injected into the task list"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks must record when they are created and changed, but code under `src/domain/` may not read the clock (r3).
+
+## Decision
+
+`createTaskList` takes a `clock: () => string` returning an ISO-8601 date-time, and passes its reading to
+the task functions as `now`. The public `createTodoList` defaults the clock to the system clock
+(`new Date().toISOString()`), the only place the clock is read; tests pass a stepping clock.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The domain stays deterministic and testable. `createTaskList` now has a required parameter. Each change
+reads the clock once.
